[{:db/id "q-75944/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "db3a4b60-1da6-552b-bfc5-1901fe77a653" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75944/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "c2fbd998-d8fa-5fe5-80dc-8e18f7f32669" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75944/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "233c4437-c3c7-5c42-8159-06e4c89f17e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75944/selection/ca37ca5c52d4082a138d9a3a77acab9a9a5cfca994ee6b1ddec0924a2fd4f821" :answer/id #uuid "4cbaada4-460b-53e7-b10f-d1407f49b7a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{{}{d}_{1},{d}_{2}\\text{}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(D)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75944/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "db7a6b0b-fefd-528b-a7a9-fc835fc2cc15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75944/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "09ba8c88-4ec9-533e-8915-61b77a478f4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75944/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-75944/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-75944/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-75944/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-75944/selection/ca37ca5c52d4082a138d9a3a77acab9a9a5cfca994ee6b1ddec0924a2fd4f821" "q-75944/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75944" :question/id #uuid "818d46d8-053e-504e-a7ef-dda21646e836" :question/math-academy-id "q-75944" :question/problem "The matrix $D$ is given below. Let ${d}_{1}$, ${d}_{2}$, and ${d}_{3}$ be the respective columns of $D.$ Determine if $B=\\text{{}{d}_{1},{d}_{2}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(D).$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${d}_{3}={x}_{1}{d}_{1}+{x}_{2}{d}_{2}.$\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -7 & -17\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $D$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -7 & -17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-\\frac{1}{8}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(D)$ is ${{d}_{1},{d}_{2}},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nNow, since the $3$rd column of the reduced matrix is a non-pivot column, then the entries in that column tell us the coefficients needed to express ${d}_{3}$ as a linear combination of all the other columns in the original matrix. So, we have\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{d}_{3}}={{(3)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{d}_{1}}+{{(2)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{d}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=3\\cdot 2=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-75944/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db27967e-f80c-587b-9b10-28f1a5518f57"] :knowledge-poi