db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75956" :question/id #uuid "57b347bf-9941-5eb7-880e-06ec4f0acd68" :question/math-academy-id "q-75956" :question/problem "The matrix $W$ is given below. Let ${w}_{1}$, ${w}_{2}$, and ${w}_{3}$ be the respective columns of $W.$\nDetermine if $B=\\text{{}{w}_{1},{w}_{3}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(W).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${w}_{2}={x}_{1}{w}_{1}+{x}_{3}{w}_{3}.$\n\n$$\nW=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $W$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $3$rd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(W)$ is ${{w}_{1},{w}_{3}},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nNow, since the $2$nd column of the reduced matrix is a non-pivot column, then the entries in that column tell us the coefficients needed to express ${w}_{2}$ as a linear combination of all the other columns in the original matrix. So, we have\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{w}_{2}}={{(-3)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{w}_{1}}+{{(0)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{3}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{w}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}=(-3)\\cdot 0=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-75956/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db27967e-f80c-587b-9b10-28f1a5518f57"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75956"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75980/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "70e03ed2-c04f-5ac6-9481-08ad33c0d6c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75980/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "0d0bfe15-577b-512f-8bb4-24cafdb791b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75980/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "af9422e0-df30-5156-84a4-dd2d595fdc25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75980/selection/7cf1c115b3321c819af8976053af6fc757454dd94e20b7824440da46faf02a6d" :answer/id #uuid "25814223-9f1a-5872-9169-7741a7a797c8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${{v}_{1},{v}_{3}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(V)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75980/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "8621ce1a-9fa9-5d25-94c4-ad650d7bcdac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75980/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8348dac4-cf4b-5637-952a-2b86f5a9be47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75980/selection/7cf1c115b3321c819af8976053af6fc757454dd94e20b7824440da46faf02a6d" :answer-field/choices ["q-75980/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-75980/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" "q-75980/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-75980/selection/7cf1c115b3321c819af8976053af6fc757454dd94e20b7824440da46faf02a6d" "q-75980/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75980" :question/id #uuid "d0a98068-9a46-5034-95cd-31840e044295" :question/math-academy-id "q-75980" :question/problem "The matrix $V$ is given below. Let ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2}$,  ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$ be the respective columns of $V.$\nDetermine if $B=\\text{{}{v}_{1},{v}_{3}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(V).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${v}_{2}={x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}.$ \n\n$$\nV=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & -6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 20 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $V$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & -6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 20 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 20 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 20 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{10}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(V)$ is ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{4}}.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{3}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(V).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-75980/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3bf9ea3-d57f-53f6-aa3c-eddffe1a8cfa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75980"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-111468/selection/3f6b6ccb3ec5c7440022fcd29237e6ce0c6df1101709f9c80e7d21b